descriptions.description:
We build blowing-up solutions to the critical elliptic system with Neumann boundary condition,
 \begin{equation*}
 \begin{cases}
 -Δu_1 + λu_1 = u_1^{3} -βu_1u_2^2 &amp; \text{in } Ω,
 -Δu_2 + λu_2 = u_2^{3} -βu_1^2u_2 &amp; \text{in } Ω,
 \frac{\partial u_1}{\partialν} = \frac{\partial u_2}{\partialν} = 0, &amp; \text{on } \partial Ω,
 \end{cases}
 \end{equation*}
 when $λ&gt;0$ is sufficiently large in a competitive regime (i.e. $ β&gt;0$) and in a domain $Ω\subset\mathbb R^4$ with smooth protrusions.
